## 📄 **1. تعديل الفيتشر — `fetch-icons.js`**

**تعديل دالة `normalizeFill`:**

```javascript
function normalizeFill(svgContent) {
  // Case 1: root <svg> has fill/color attribute
  const rootFillMatch = svgContent.match(/<svg[^>]*\s(fill|color)="([^"]+)"/i);

  if (rootFillMatch) {
    const color = rootFillMatch[2];
    let cleaned = svgContent.replace(
      new RegExp(`\\s${rootFillMatch[1]}="${color}"`, 'i'),
      ''
    );
    cleaned = cleaned.replace(
      /<(path|circle|rect|polygon|polyline|line|ellipse)([^>]*?)(\/?)>/gi,
      (match, tag, attrs, selfClose) => {
        if (/\sfill=/i.test(attrs) || /\sstyle=/i.test(attrs)) return match;
        return `<${tag}${attrs} fill="${color}"${selfClose}>`;
      }
    );
    return cleaned;
  }

  // Case 2: no fill anywhere → check if any element has fill
  const hasAnyFill = /<(path|circle|rect|polygon|polyline|line|ellipse)[^>]*\sfill=/i.test(svgContent);

  if (!hasAnyFill) {
    // No fill at all → add currentColor to all shape elements
    return svgContent.replace(
      /<(path|circle|rect|polygon|polyline|line|ellipse)([^>]*?)(\/?)>/gi,
      (match, tag, attrs, selfClose) => {
        if (/\sfill=/i.test(attrs) || /\sstyle=/i.test(attrs)) return match;
        return `<${tag}${attrs} fill="currentColor"${selfClose}>`;
      }
    );
  }

  // Case 3: has fills on some elements → leave as is
  return svgContent;
}
```

**المكان:** نفس الدالة اللي عندك، بتستبدلها بالنسخة دي.

